      </pub-date>
      <pub-date pub-type="collection">
        <year>{{ pub_year }}</year>
      </pub-date>

      <!-- ── Abstract ── -->
      <abstract>
        <p>We present a genome assembly from a{% if specimen_sex %} {{ specimen_sex }}{% endif %} specimen of
          <italic>{{ species_name }}</italic>, the {{ common_name }}
          ({{ higher_taxonomy }}). The genome assembly includes two haplotypes
          with total lengths of {{ hap1_total_length_mb }} and
          {{ hap2_total_length_mb }} megabases. Both haplotypes are
          chromosome-level (2n={{ chromosome_count }}) with
          {{ hap1_pct_assigned }}% of scaffolds assigned to chromosomes in
          haplotype 1 and {{ hap2_pct_assigned }}% assigned in haplotype 2.
          The mitochondrial genome has also been assembled, with a length of
          {{ mito_length_kb }} kilobases.</p>
      </abstract>

      <kwd-group kwd-group-type="author">
        <kwd><italic>{{ species_name }}</italic></kwd>
        <kwd>{{ common_name }}</kwd>
        <kwd>genome sequence</kwd>
        <kwd>chromosomal</kwd>
        <kwd>{{ order }}</kwd>
      </kwd-group>

      <funding-group>
        <award-group id="fund-1">
          <funding-source>Minderoo Foundation</funding-source>
          <award-id>OceanOmics</award-id>
        </award-group>
        <funding-statement>This work was supported by the Minderoo Foundation
          through the OceanOmics initiative.</funding-statement>
      </funding-group>
    </article-meta>
  </front>

  <!-- ============================================================
       BODY
       ============================================================ -->
  <body>

    <!-- ── Species taxonomy ── -->
    <sec>
      <title>Species taxonomy</title>
      <p>{{ full_taxonomy_string }} <italic>{{ species_name }}</italic> ({{ authority }}) (NCBI:txid{{ ncbi_taxid }})</p>
    </sec>

    <!-- ── Background ── (MANUAL ENTRY — species-specific) -->
    <sec>
      <title>Background</title>
      <!-- INSERT SPECIES BACKGROUND HERE -->
      {{ background_paragraphs }}
      <p>Here, we present a chromosome-level, haplotype-resolved genome
        assembly of the {{ common_name }},
        <italic>{{ species_name }}</italic>. The sequence was derived from a
        {% if specimen_sex %}{{ specimen_sex }} {% endif %}specimen (<xref ref-type="fig" rid="f1">Figure 1</xref>),
        collected from {{ collection_location }}.</p>

      <!-- Figure 1: Specimen photograph -->
      <fig fig-type="figure" id="f1" orientation="portrait" position="float">
        <label>Figure 1. </label>
        <caption>
          <title>Photograph of the
            <italic>{{ species_name }}</italic> ({{ tolid }}) specimen used
            for genome sequencing.</title>
        </caption>
        <graphic orientation="portrait" position="float"
                 xlink:href="{{ specimen_photo_path }}"/>
      </fig>
    </sec>

    <!-- ── Methods ── -->
    <sec sec-type="methods">
      <title>Methods</title>

      <sec>
        <title>Sample acquisition</title>
        <p>An adult{% if specimen_sex %} {{ specimen_sex }}{% endif %}
          <italic>{{ species_name }}</italic> (ToLID {{ tolid }}) was collected
          from {{ collection_location }} (latitude {{ latitude }},
          longitude {{ longitude }}) on {{ collection_date }}. The specimen was
          collected by {{ collector_names }} from the {{ institution }}
          ({{ institution_abbrev }}) on {{ collection_method }}. The specimen
          {% if formal_voucher %}was {{ preservation_method }} and subsequently accessioned into the
          {{ institution_abbrev }} as
          <italic>{{ species_name }}</italic> voucher ID {{ voucher_id }}.{% else %}is held at the {{ institution }} ({{ institution_abbrev }}).{% endif %}</p>
      </sec>

      <sec>
        <title>DNA extraction, library preparation and sequencing</title>
        <p>High molecular weight (HMW) genomic DNA was extracted from
          approximately 25 mg of {{ hifi_tissue }} tissue. Tissue was
          homogenised using the TissueRuptor II (QIAGEN, Hilden, Germany)
          and then pelleted as per the PacBio Nanobind tissue kit
          (PacBio, CA, USA) protocol. Cell lysis and DNA isolation were
          performed following the PacBio &#x201c;Extracting HMW DNA from
          skeletal muscle using Nanobind&#x201d; procedure (102-579-200,
          Dec 2022). The quantity and fragment length distribution of
          extracted gDNA were
          determined using a Qubit 3 Fluorometer with the Qubit dsDNA
          Broad-Range Assay Kit (Thermo Fisher Scientific, MA, USA), a
          NanoDrop One (Thermo Fisher Scientific, MA, USA) and a Femto Pulse
          with the Genomic DNA 165kb kit (Agilent, CA, USA). A PacBio HiFi
          SMRTbell&#x00ae; library was prepared using the PacBio SMRTbell&#x00ae;
          prep kit 3.0 according to manufacturer&#x2019;s instructions. The
          library was sequenced on a {{ pacbio_platform }}.</p>
      </sec>

      <sec>
        <title>Hi-C library construction and sequencing</title>
        <p>Cryogenic grinding of flash-frozen {{ hic_tissue }} tissue in liquid
          nitrogen was used to facilitate the construction of a
          {{ hic_lib_type }} library, using the {{ hic_prep_module }} and
          Dovetail Library Module for Illumina kits (Cantata Bio, CA, USA) as
          per the manufacturer&#x2019;s protocols.{% if hic_shallow_platform %}
          Shallow sequencing of the Hi-C libraries was performed on a
          {{ hic_shallow_platform }} platform using a 2 &#x00d7; 150 bp
          paired-end run to assess library complexity.{% endif %}
          Deep sequencing of Hi-C data was carried out on a
          {{ hic_deep_platform }} platform with a 2 &#x00d7; 150 bp
          paired-end run configuration to generate chromosome conformation
          data.</p>
      </sec>

      {% if rna_tissues %}
      <sec>
        <title>RNA extraction, library construction and sequencing</title>
        <p>Flash-frozen {{ rna_tissues }} tissue from the same specimen was
          used for RNA extraction using the RNeasy&#x00ae; Fibrous Tissue Mini
          Kit (Qiagen, Germany) according to the manufacturer&#x2019;s
          instructions. RNA concentration was quantified using a
          Qubit&#x2122; fluorometer with the Qubit&#x2122; RNA High
          Sensitivity (HS) Assay Kit (Thermo Fisher Scientific, USA) and
          cross-checked with a NanoDrop&#x2122; spectrophotometer (Thermo
          Fisher Scientific, USA). RNA integrity and fragment size distribution
          were assessed on an Agilent TapeStation system using the appropriate
          RNA ScreenTape assay (Agilent Technologies, USA). Total RNA extracted
          from {{ rna_tissues }} from the same individual was used as input for
          the Iso-Seq Express 2.0 Kit (Pacific Biosciences, USA) in separate
          reactions to generate barcoded full-length cDNA, following the
          manufacturer&#x2019;s instructions. The resulting full-length cDNA
          libraries for each tissue were then processed independently using the
          PacBio Kinnex&#x2122; full-length RNA Kit (Pacific Biosciences, USA)
          to produce concatenated SMRTbell&#x00ae; libraries for Iso-Seq
          analysis. Kinnex libraries were sequenced on a PacBio Revio system
          (Pacific Biosciences, USA).</p>
      </sec>
      {% endif %}

    </sec>

    <!-- ── Genome assembly, curation and evaluation ── -->
    <sec>
      <title>Genome assembly, curation and evaluation</title>

      <sec>
        <title>Assembly</title>
          <p>Raw PacBio HiFi reads were quality-assessed using FastQC
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-andrews2010">Andrews, 2010</xref>)
            and adapter-filtered using HiFiAdapterFilt
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-sim2022">Sim
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2022</xref>), which uses BBMap
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-bushnell2014">Bushnell,
              2014</xref>) internally for alignment.</p>
          <p>Prior to assembly of the PacBio HiFi reads, a database of k-mer
            counts (k&#x2009;=&#x2009;31) was generated from the filtered reads
            using Meryl (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-rhie2020">Rhie
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2020</xref>). GenomeScope2
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-ranallo2020">Ranallo-Benavidez
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2020</xref>) was used to analyse the
            k-mer frequency distributions, providing estimates of genome size,
            heterozygosity, homozygosity, and repeat content. The HiFi reads
            were assembled using Hifiasm
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-cheng2021">Cheng
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2021, 2022</xref>) in Hi-C phasing mode,
            resulting in a pair of haplotype-resolved assemblies. Initial
            assembly quality statistics were generated with Gfastats
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-formenti2022">Formenti
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2022</xref>), BUSCO
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-manni2021">Manni
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2021</xref>) and MerquryFK
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-rhie2020">Rhie
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2020</xref>).</p>
          <p>Hi-C reads were mapped to the primary contigs using the OMNIC
            pipeline (Cantata Bio, CA, USA), with alignment performed using
            BWA-MEM (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-li2009bwa">Li &amp; Durbin,
              2009</xref>) and contact extraction using pairtools
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-open2c2024">Open2C
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2024</xref>). Scaffolding was performed by YaHs
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-zhou2023">Zhou
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2023</xref>) using the
            --no-contig-ec option to prevent over-fragmentation of the input
            contigs. The scaffolded assemblies were decontaminated using NCBI
            FCS-GX and Tiara
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-karlicki2022">Karlicki
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2022</xref>) for mitochondrion contamination. The resulting
            decontaminated assemblies were evaluated using Gfastats
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-formenti2022">Formenti
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2022</xref>), BUSCO
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-manni2021">Manni
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2021</xref>) and MerquryFK
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-rhie2020">Rhie
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2020</xref>). TIDK
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-brown2025">Brown
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2025</xref>) was used to predict
            telomeres in the assemblies and BEDtools
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-quinlan2010">Quinlan &amp; Hall,
              2010</xref>) was used to generate coverage and gaps tracks
            injected into Pretext Maps
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-harry2022">Harry, 2022</xref>)
            to prepare the genome for manual curation. Processing of the
            assembly was done using the Nextflow
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-ewels2020">Ewels
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2020</xref>) pipeline
            <ext-link ext-link-type="uri"
              xlink:href="https://github.com/Minderoo-OceanOmics-Centre-UWA/OceanOmics-OceanGenomes-ref-genomes"
              >OceanOmics-OceanGenomes-ref-genomes.v1.0.0</ext-link>, using tools
            containerised with Singularity
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-kurtzer2017">Kurtzer
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2017</xref>).</p>
          <p>The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-uliano2023">Uliano-Silva
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2023</xref>), which runs MitoFinder
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-allio2020">Allio
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2020</xref>), and uses these annotations
            to select the final mitochondrial contig and to ensure the general
            quality of the sequence.</p>
        </sec>

        <sec>
          <title>Curation</title>
          <p>Manual curation was conducted using PretextView
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-harry2022">Harry, 2022</xref>),
            with additional insights provided by BUSCO-based synteny plots
            (chromsyn). Scaffolds were visually inspected and corrected as
            described by Howe <italic>et al.</italic>
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-howe2021">2021</xref>). Any
            identified contamination, missed joins, and mis-joins were
            corrected, and duplicate sequences were tagged and removed.</p>
        </sec>

        <sec>
          <title>Evaluation of the final assembly</title>
          <p>The MerquryFK tool
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-rhie2020">Rhie
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2020</xref>) was used to evaluate
            k-mer completeness and assembly quality for the curated haplotypes,
            using the k-mer databases (k&#x2009;=&#x2009;31) computed before
            genome assembly. The analysis outputs included k-mer plots, assembly
            QV scores and completeness statistics. Gfastats
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-formenti2022">Formenti
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2022</xref>) was used to assess
            contiguity and BUSCO
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-manni2021">Manni
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2021</xref>) was used to assess
            completeness of the assemblies.</p>
          <p>The final assembly was also analysed with BlobToolKit
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-challis2020">Challis
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2020</xref>) using the
            OceanOmics-OceanGenomes-genomenotes pipeline. It aligned the HiFi
            and Hi-C reads to the assemblies using minimap2
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-li2018">Li, 2018</xref>) and
            SAMtools (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-li2009sam">Li
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2009</xref>) and generated coverage
            tracks for regions of fixed size (1 kb). BUSCO genes were counted
            in regions of fixed size (1 kb) and stats were calculated per
            window to assess GC and AT content. In parallel, the assembly was
            chunked with Seqkit and split into sliding windows of 100,000 kb.
            The chunks were aligned to the core_nt database using BLAST+
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-camacho2009">Camacho
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2009</xref>) to screen for any
            additional contamination. The resulting files were used as input to
            generate a blobdir for visualisation. Quality control outputs across
            the pipeline were aggregated using MultiQC
            (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="ref-ewels2016">Ewels
              <italic>et al.</italic>, 2016</xref>).</p>
        </sec>
    </sec>

    <!-- ── Genome sequence report ── -->
    <sec>
      <title>Genome sequence report</title>

      <sec>
        <title>Sequencing data</title>
        <p>The genome of an adult{% if specimen_sex %} {{ specimen_sex }}{% endif %}
          <italic>{{ species_name }}</italic> was sequenced using Pacific
          Biosciences single-molecule HiFi long reads, generating a total of
          {{ hifi_gb }} Gb (gigabases) of HiFi data from {{ hifi_read_count }}
          reads. Chromosome conformation Hi-C sequencing produced
          {{ hic_gb }} Gb of data from {{ hic_read_count }} reads. The raw
          sequence data obtained is summarised in
          <xref ref-type="table" rid="T1">Table 1</xref>.</p>
        <p>GenomeScope k-mer profiling (k&#x2009;=&#x2009;31) of the raw
          PacBio HiFi data estimated the haploid genome to be
          {{ genomescope_size_bp }} bp. Heterozygosity was estimated at
          {{ heterozygosity_pct }}% and repeat content was
          {{ repeat_size_bp }} bp
          (<xref ref-type="fig" rid="f2">Figure 2</xref>). The coverage of
          the PacBio sequencing was {{ hifi_coverage }}x and the Hi-C was
          {{ hic_coverage }}x.</p>

        <!-- Figure 2: GenomeScope k-mer profile -->
        <fig fig-type="figure" id="f2" orientation="portrait" position="float">
          <label>Figure 2. </label>
          <caption>
            <title>GenomeScope2 k-mer frequency plot for
              <italic>{{ species_name }}</italic>.</title>
            <p>K-mer frequency distribution (k&#x2009;=&#x2009;31) of the raw
              PacBio HiFi reads plotted using GenomeScope2. The x-axis shows
              k-mer coverage depth and the y-axis shows the frequency of k-mers
              at each depth. Peaks correspond to heterozygous and homozygous
              sequence fractions. Estimated genome size:
              {{ genomescope_size_mb }} Mb; heterozygosity:
              {{ heterozygosity_pct }}%; repeat content:
              {{ repeat_size_bp }} bp.</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic orientation="portrait" position="float"
                   xlink:href="{{ genomescope_plot_path }}"/>
        </fig>

        <!-- Table 1: Raw sequencing data -->
        <table-wrap id="T1" orientation="portrait" position="anchor">
          <label>Table 1. </label>
          <caption>
            <title>Sequence data information for the genome assembly of
              <italic>{{ species_name }}</italic>. ToLID refers to the unique
              identifier assigned to the specimen. BioSample describes the
              biological source material from which the data were generated,
              and the run accessions refer to the identifiers assigned to the
              raw sequencing reads for each dataset.</title>
          </caption>
          <table content-type="article-table" frame="hsides">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top"></th>
                <th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">PacBio HiFi</th>
                <th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">Hi-C</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">ToLID</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ tolid }}</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ tolid }}</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">Tissue</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hifi_tissue }}</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hic_tissue }}</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">Sequencing platform</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ pacbio_platform }}</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hic_platform }}</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">BioSample</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hifi_biosample }}</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hic_biosample }}</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">Run accessions</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hifi_run_accession }}</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hic_run_accession }}</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">Read count total</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hifi_read_count }}</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hic_read_count }}</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">Base count total</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hifi_gb }} Gb</td>
                <td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1" valign="top">{{ hic_gb }} Gb</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </table-wrap>
      </sec>

      <sec>
        <title>Assembly statistics</title>
        <p>Haplotype 1 and Haplotype 2 were assembled using Hi-C phasing and
          scaffolded, the two haplotypes were combined for manual curation. The
          resulting curated assemblies were processed through the OceanOmics
          post-curation pipeline (<ext-link ext-link-type="uri"
            xlink:href="https://github.com/Minderoo-OceanOmics-Centre-UWA/OceanOmics-OceanGenomes-post-curation/tree/master"
            >OceanOmics-OceanGenomes-post-curation</ext-link>) for
          quality checks.</p>
        <p>The final haplotype 1 assembly had a total length of
          {{ hap1_total_length_mb }} Mb, with a scaffold N50 of
          {{ hap1_scaffold_n50_mb }} Mb and {{ hap1_num_gaps }} gaps
          (<xref ref-type="table" rid="T2">Table 2</xref>).</p>
        <p>A total of {{ hap1_pct_assigned }}% of scaffolds were assigned to
          {{ hap1_num_autosomes }} autosomal chromosomes. Chromosome-scale
          scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data are named in order of size
          (<xref ref-type="fig" rid="f3">Figure 3</xref>).</p>
        <p>The mitochondrial genome was also assembled and has been submitted as
          a standalone record to GenBank.</p>

